[[:db/retract 17592186246854 :answer-field/choices 17592186244768] [:db/retract 17592186246854 :answer-field/choices 17592186246449] [:db/retract 17592186246854 :answer-field/choices 17592186245003] [:db/retract 17592186246854 :answer-field/choices 17592186246052] [:db/retract 17592186246854 :answer-field/choices 17592186244955] [:db/retract 17592186316712 :answer-field/choices 17592186315186] [:db/retract 17592186316712 :answer-field/choices 17592186315427] [:db/retract 17592186316712 :answer-field/choices 17592186315318] [:db/retract 17592186316712 :answer-field/choices 17592186316086] [:db/retract 17592186316712 :answer-field/choices 17592186315708] [:db/retract 17592186344690 :answer-field/choices 17592186342914] [:db/retract 17592186344612 :answer-field/choices 17592186342804] {:db/id 17592186119815 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-293eb96a-a168-5847-97d0-8739c8726172"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119673 :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $\\mathcal{B}$ is indeed a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3,\\mathbf{a}_4 \\}.$ So, we want to find $x_1, x_2, x_3 \\in \\mathbb{R}$ such that \n![](images/79/79525b86cbbbc191f9a19ffa817fdaebeb0d1f6bd99eb97ce3f642a7fdf6033e.svg)\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $\\mathcal{B}$ is indeed a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,\\mathbf{a}_3,\\mathbf{a}_4 \\}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that $x_1=-5,$ $x_2=0,$ and $x_3=7,$ meaning that\n![](images/c7/c732a274f27d98231f9a94dad40ff15f53e82f00b076ba46464ac640c2765703.svg)\n\nTherefore, $x_1 + x_2 +  x_3 = (-5) + 0 + 7 = 2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247170 :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$  by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{3}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}=0\\cdot {a}_{1}+(-1)\\cdot {a}_{2}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{3}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is spanned by just $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}},{{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186246854 :answer-field/correct "answer-c96b69bc-01bd-5856-808f-355764eb3024" :answer-field/choices ["answer-36398b63-dad4-5688-8a66-fe0da922b660" "answer-892d14b4-33ce-5d53-88a8-6c11d10a6e6a" "answer-c96b69bc-01bd-5856-808f-355764eb3024" "answer-432a4bca-b02b-564d-8440-b892a8cece98" "answer-3302cac0-c190-588a-bf1e-1dcf4b11b461"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36398b63-dad4-5688-8a66-fe0da922b660" :answer/id #uuid "36398b63-dad4-5688-8a66-fe0da922b660" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-892d14b4-33ce-5d53-88a8-6c11d10a6e6a" :answer/id #uuid "892d14b4-33ce-5d53-88a8-6c11d10a6e6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c96b69bc-01bd-5856-808f-355764eb3024" :answer/id #uuid "c96b69bc-01bd-5856-808f-355764eb3024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-432a4bca-b02b-564d-8440-b892a8cece98" :answer/id #uuid "432a4bca-b02b-564d-8440-b892a8cece98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3302cac0-c190-588a-bf1e-1dcf4b11b461" :answer/id #uuid "3302cac0-c190-588a-bf1e-1dcf4b11b461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-293eb96a-a168-5847-97d0-8739c8726172" :question/id #uuid "293eb96a-a168-5847-97d0-8739c8726172" :question/math-academy-id "q-74977" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{1}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=1\\cdot {a}_{2}+1\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{1}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is spanned by just $\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set $\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}},{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9ccdc12a-fbdf-5044-b512-ae9ee21b3e92"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9ccdc12a-fbdf-5044-b512-ae9ee21b3e92" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ccdc12a-fbdf-5044-b512-ae9ee21b3e92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5065bce1-b0d9-5de9-83b0-c30228b25991" :answer-field/choices ["answer-77805aee-b005-52d0-a725-17ced8ae5682" "answer-9d88a0d5-9800-59a9-a10a-33be5d1d8e49" "answer-0ad3f32a-699b-5f19-8537-5ee75cb30b47" "answer-5065bce1-b0d9-5de9-83b0-c30228b25991" "answer-acf57914-2b95-5f27-9687-899336a28991"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77805aee-b005-52d0-a725-17ced8ae5682" :answer/id #uuid "77805aee-b005-52d0-a725-17ced8ae5682" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d88a0d5-9800-59a9-a10a-33be5d1d8e49" :answer/id #uuid "9d88a0d5-9800-59a9-a10a-33be5d1d8e49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ad3f32a-699b-5f19-8537-5ee75cb30b47" :answer/id #uuid "0ad3f32a-699b-5f19-8537-5ee75cb30b47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5065bce1-b0d9-5de9-83b0-c30228b25991" :answer/id #uuid "5065bce1-b0d9-5de9-83b0-c30228b25991" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acf57914-2b95-5f27-9687-899336a28991" :answer/id #uuid "acf57914-2b95-5f27-9687-899336a28991" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317510 :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316712 :answer-field/correct "answer-29b21dda-de01-5604-87d6-f584e72f6811" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e75b98ee-ddb1-5ceb-8b26-88ce2b2c42d9" "answer-682a6b44-ab7e-500b-bb7e-d04456824f16" "answer-29b21dda-de01-5604-87d6-f584e72f6811" "answer-a7beabae-c19b-5ab1-bf80-b342b52cb235" "answer-aaa02ece-075b-5a23-8ec8-b922ddb2aea1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e75b98ee-ddb1-5ceb-8b26-88ce2b2c42d9" :answer/id #uuid "e75b98ee-ddb1-5ceb-8b26-88ce2b2c42d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-682a6b44-ab7e-500b-bb7e-d04456824f16" :answer/id #uuid "682a6b44-ab7e-500b-bb7e-d04456824f16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29b21dda-de01-5604-87d6-f584e72f6811" :answer/id #uuid "29b21dda-de01-5604-87d6-f584e72f6811" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7beabae-c19b-5ab1-bf80-b342b52cb235" :answer/id #uuid "a7beabae-c19b-5ab1-bf80-b342b52cb235" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aaa02ece-075b-5a23-8ec8-b922ddb2aea1" :answer/id #uuid "aaa02ece-075b-5a23-8ec8-b922ddb2aea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345207 :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=-4,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+(-4)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-2)\\cdot (-4)=8.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186344690 :answer-field/choices ["answer-8d2d9553-3fcc-5436-9ae5-e9313490ab61"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d2d9553-3fcc-5436-9ae5-e9313490ab61" :answer/id #uuid "8d2d9553-3fcc-5436-9ae5-e9313490ab61" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120524 :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ ${a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B=\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3},$ where ${a}_{4}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-8,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=7,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-8)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+7\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-8+0+7=-1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186344612 :answer-field/choices ["answer-931fbf19-90fd-5095-9ed2-228296291e7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-931fbf19-90fd-5095-9ed2-228296291e7d" :answer/id #uuid "931fbf19-90fd-5095-9ed2-228296291e7d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}\\}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
